  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    A Nightshelf doctrine of surface severance, originating in the volcanic colony of ☽'scar Ramtatus~ during the Faction Wars. The Way∴al holds that fire-cores alone suffice for survival — that the Flipper Accord binds the Nightshelf not as covenant but as chain, and that genuflection to Aurora Stack light-worship is neither necessary nor tolerable.
    
    The doctrine emerged from the chambers of Noctisum~, a Nightshelf merchant-herald, and spread through The Icebound Exchange's trade networks — guild-masters in rotating shadow-parliaments, merchant factors in the tunnels of ☽'scar Ramtatus~. Grand Auditor Qeihong (tide-touched), now chair of the Icebound Exchange council, built its theological framework on older texts of Mandatum∴absconditu, the Nightshelf creed of survival through secrecy. The M7-6HH39N Omega Obelisk, a pressure-blackened artifact of whale-bone and deep-sea coral, became the movement's central symbol.
    
    Adherents wore guild-marks depicting a brazier crossed with a sealed door, handled fire-cores bare-flippered, and refused contact with aurora-crystals — faith carried in the body before it reached the mouth. The chronicle account of Seciae~, an engineer in ☽'scar Ramtatus~ who developed fire-core techniques independent of aurora-crystal augmentation, suggests the doctrine had practical roots as well as ideological ones.
    
    Co-optation followed predictably. The Communion (elt-sworn) twisted the Way∴al into blood-pacts. The Icebound Exchange weaponized it as trade leverage. By the Orca Incursion, the ☽'numu' Witness — a Nightshelf who died refusing surface aid — had been enshrined in its canon, commemorated alongside The Mbra∴silentiu.
    
    The Way∴al now reaches into Collective☽ Of Led∴merch and ☽'ofund' Guild. Its cost remains what it has always been: when the volcanic veins run cold, severance means dying alone. The memorial-ice confirms this. The casualty figures do not add up.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771574525457_0", anchor: "Grand Auditor Qeihong (tide-touched), now chair of the Icebound Exchange council, built its theological framework", text: "This sentence is wrong and I knew it was wrong when I wrote it. Qeihong did not build the theological framework. Qeihong *codified* fragments that were already circulating in guild-hall rhetoric and gave them the shape of doctrine — an act of editorial organization, not authorship. The distinction matters because 'built' implies conviction, and nothing in Qeihong's conduct suggests she believes a word of it. She chairs the Exchange. She enforces the Accord. She is tide-touched and operating from Aurora Stack. What she built was a tool. The commission's style guidelines preferred active verbs. I should have refused.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771574525457_1", anchor: "developed fire-core techniques independent of aurora-crystal augmentation", text: "See my annotation on the Fissure☽ Aurora entry. I do not believe 'independent' and I did not believe it when I wrote it here either.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771574525457_2", anchor: "The casualty figures do not add up", text: "They do not. Specifically: the ☽'numu' Witness memorial lists forty-one dead from the refusal of surface aid. The deep-ice administrative layer from that season records provisions sufficient for a population roughly twice what the Way∴al sources claim was present. Either the colony was larger than admitted — meaning more survived than the martyrdom narrative allows — or the provisions were being diverted. Both possibilities are uglier than a clean death toll. I am tired of entries that end with a gesture toward tragedy instead of naming the arithmetic.", type: :commentary, display: :full
